{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:76c414494c9fabef","name":"Imperial Sentinel","source":{"id":"source:reference-76c414494c9fabef","title":"Imperial Sentinel","revision":19475,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T22:02:41Z","sha256":"886f8f1fcdda18a3de0fec907f97f154c9be9f3591b4702ee7b43e597ece8324","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19475","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Imperial%20Sentinel&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-76c414494c9fabef","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Unleashed Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Unleashed_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Senate Guard"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Senate_Guard","referenceId":"reference:e0e53bb7c97f9801"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Empire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Empire","referenceId":"reference:f9c9a48674cc3415"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Imperial Sentinels are among the most mysterious of the Emperor's agents. To date, only a handful of these mute, armored giants have briefly appeared in public, usually to take custody of particular prisoners (often Jedi) while in transit to Imperial Center or secret locations. Some speculate that the Sentinels are ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droids","referenceId":"reference:6e72e583603b9ea8"}," or an alien ",{"tag":"a","children":["Species"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Species","referenceId":"reference:56205e12c20fb568"},", though the latter theory is discounted given the Empire's new antialien agenda.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The truth is far darker than any people suspect. The Sentinels are an early experiment of the Emperor and his inner circle of Dark Side users to develop a class of beings completely subservient to their will. Using hidden cloning facilities on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Byss"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Byss?action=edit&redlink=1"},", they corrupt a clone's development physically and through ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Dark Side"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Dark_Side"}," of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"},", creating a huge, strong, but nearly mindless individual completely subservient to its masters. Since they are in the early stages of development, it is rare for Sentinels to be seen outside of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Byss"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Byss?action=edit&redlink=1"},". However, they are occasionally brought forth to take custody of Force-using prisoners or for limited field-testing.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The inner circle estimates it will be decades before control of the Sentinels will be fine-tuned enough for their widespread use, appropriately about the time the other denizens of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Byss"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Byss?action=edit&redlink=1"}," are expected to be ready for their galactic deployment.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Imperial Sentinel Statistics (CL 2)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Large ",{"tag":"a","children":["Human"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Human","referenceId":"reference:9ffa865f2bc6e850"}," (Modified) ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," 6\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Dark Side Score"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dark_Side_Score"},":"]}," 6\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +1